# Security headers for the Cloudflare Pages deployment (added in the
# 2026-09-30 vulnerability audit). Cloudflare merges these with its own
# defaults (x-content-type-options, referrer-policy are already set upstream).
#
# IMPORTANT: the Content-Security-Policy pins the inline preloader <script>
# in index.html by SHA-256 hash. If that script is ever edited, recompute:
#   python3 -c "
#   import re,hashlib,base64
#   s = open('index.html', encoding='utf-8').read()
#   m = re.search(r'<script>(.*?)</script>', s, re.S)
#   print('sha256-' + base64.b64encode(hashlib.sha256(m.group(1).encode()).digest()).decode())"
# and replace the hash below, otherwise the preloader will stop running.
#
# External origins, each tied to a real in-repo feature (2026-11-04 pass 2):
# - script-src https://apis.google.com — Firebase Auth injects gapi
#   (api.js) for Google sign-in; it was CSP-blocked on every page, which
#   was the site-wide console error holding Best Practices at 92.
# - frame-src firebaseapp.com + accounts.google.com — the Firebase Auth
#   helper iframe (authDomain/__/auth/iframe) and the gapi accounts
#   iframe; frame-src 'none' silently killed both.
# - frame-src https://www.instagram.com — the homepage reel embed
#   (InstagramReel component), also dead under frame-src 'none'.
# - googletagmanager / google-analytics — the env-gated, consent-gated
#   GA4 loader in src/lib/analytics.ts (inert until the owner sets
#   VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID; allowed now so enabling it can't break).
# No 'unsafe-inline'/'unsafe-eval' for scripts; origins stay explicit.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-NMLzoW6aV926ihb3CK7x4OVlz71i8nJw8eJI1DVjXuE=' https://apis.google.com https://www.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https:; media-src 'self' data: https:; connect-src 'self' https://firestore.googleapis.com https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com https://securetoken.googleapis.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://www.googletagmanager.com; frame-src https://gen-lang-client-0970693213.firebaseapp.com https://accounts.google.com https://www.instagram.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()

# Cache static assets aggressively (added 2026-10-08 performance fix).
# Vite hashes asset filenames, so immutable caching is safe.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Image payloads under /images/ (added 2026-11-04, score-100 lane): the
# Express server (server.ts staticCacheOptions) already serves these with a
# 1-year immutable cache, but the Cloudflare Pages path had NO rule for them,
# which is what Lighthouse's "efficient cache lifetimes" audit flagged
# (~2.8-3.0 MB of homepage images re-downloaded on repeat visits). Image
# files here are content-addressed by upload (new uploads get new file
# names), so a 1-year immutable cache matches the server behaviour.
/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
